>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `xtraversedata_for_ss`

``` hol4
simpLib.xtraversedata_for_ss :
  simpLib.simpset -> Traverse.xtraverse_data
simpLib.traversedata_for_ss :
  simpLib.simpset -> Traverse.traverse_data
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Extracts the traversal data of a simpset.

`xtraversedata_for_ss ss` returns the rewriters, decision procedures,
congruence rules and limit of `ss`, paired with its subgoaler, unsafe
solvers, side-condition depth and term order, for use with
`Traverse.XTRAVERSE`. `traversedata_for_ss ss` returns the same data
without these settings, for use with `Traverse.TRAVERSE`.

Bounded rewrites (`Once`, `Ntimes`) share their remaining uses with those
of `ss`.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpLib.set_cond_depth 2
     boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> Traverse.XTRAVERSE (simpLib.xtraversedata_for_ss ss) [] “T ∧ p”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpLib.set_cond_depth),
[`Traverse.CONFIG_REDUCER`](#Traverse.CONFIG_REDUCER),
[`simpLib.mk_simpset`](#simpLib.mk_simpset).
